Subject: [PATCH 0013] SST: fuse pointwise algebra inside the base helpers

kOmegaSSTBase::correct creates long chains of scalar field temporaries.
Evaluate F1, F2, S2, GbyNu0, GbyNu, Pk, coefficient blends, effective
diffusivities and the final correctNut quotient with one cell traversal per
helper. Fuse the CDkOmega dot product, scaling and division as well. For
incompressible SST with F3 disabled, this replaces 80 algebra traversals
with 13, excluding unchanged mu/rho and nu acquisition, assignments and
source/matrix expressions. Intermediate temporaries and their memory
traffic disappear; temporary storage was already reused by many of the
old field operators, so this is not a claim of 67 fewer allocations.

Keep the scalar expression trees and operand order: in particular
(cBeta*k)*omega, (b1*F23)*sqrt(S2), (cBeta*omega)*max(...), and
coefficient*(gradK & gradOmega)/omega. Obtain dimensioned coefficient
values through the original dimensioned operations, and retain mu/rho
rather than substituting nu. Use the same Foam scalar and tensor inline
primitives. The tensor components feed multiplication operands, so fusing
symm/magSqr and devTwoSymm/dot does not create an extra multiply-add
boundary. Blending and diffusivity DO have separate multiply/add field
passes; volatile scalar products explicitly preserve rounding there with
GCC's default -ffp-contract=fast. No compiler flags or precision change.

Populate every patch face from the original stored patch operands through
the Field base, including processor patches: do not exchange the result.
Allocate calculated/constraint patch types as the original operators do.
Processor evaluateLocal is a no-op; other coupled patches can reevaluate
intermediate expressions, so keep the original geometric expression trees
whenever local boundary consistency is enabled and such a patch exists.
Keep correctLocalBoundaryConditions on the final result, as well as the
original nut boundary correction and fvOptions correction. DkEff and
DomegaEff retain their names for laplacian scheme selection.

All original virtual calls remain: the changes are within base helper
bodies, not a replacement of their call sites by base-qualified formulas.
LM, SAS and DES overrides (including F1, F23, S2, GbyNu0, GbyNu, Pk,
epsilonByk, sources and correctNut) still run, including their calls back
into the base implementations. The arithmetic is generic in the supplied
coefficients and mu/rho; no default-coefficient or incompressible-only
shortcut is introduced. F3 and decay control are still handled by their
original paths. Their constructor defaults are both false.

Keep gradient calls at their original point, with grad(k) and grad(omega)
as the same ordered argument pair (GCC 13 evaluates omega first in both
forms). Leave fvm calls, matrix expression assembly, solves, boundary
updates, bound, epsilonByk and solve-separated source evaluation alone.

Validation: GCC 13.3 -fsyntax-only with check-all.sh flags on the complete
incompressible and compressible turbulence-model registration TUs,
including LM/SAS/DES instantiations. Optimized scalar probes match staged arithmetic on two
million tuples and tensor probes match separate primitive field passes on
4,194,304 tensors, on both generic x86-64 and -march=znver3 at -O3 with
default contraction. Full case coefficient.dat equality is still to be
checked by the prepared serial/MPI harness; no speedup has been measured.
